                  <provenance type="#m s"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_1">Exeter, Devon.
                        Cathedral church of St Peter</orgName><p>Marginal marking in pencil as in
                        other Exeter MSS, e.g. Bodley 289. Compare also the decoration in Bodley
                        691, also an Exeter book.</p><p>Identifiable in the 1506 catalogue by second
                        folio (one of two copies therein with this second folio, 'quod aliter'). Its
                        size sugests that it, more probably than Bodley 708, is the '4to pastoral
                        Care' mentioned in the Benefactors' Register.</p><p>Damp damage at each end,
                        as in many books from Exeter.</p><p>Document added at the end in which the
                        prior and convent 'S. Nicholai Ex'' supplicate Bishop John (?Grandisson)
                        that John Taylere acolyte should be advanced to subdeacon.</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cat. pp. 302, 367 or
                     371</note></provenance>
               </history>
